<theodulf. carm. 28.451>	Hanc deus, hanc vates, hanc leges, hanc quoque princeps
<theodulf. carm. 28.452>	Percensent, haec vis pectora nostra regat.
<theodulf. carm. 28.453>	Si nos illa regat, populos tunc rite regemus,
<theodulf. carm. 28.454>	Mens bene cuncta regit, quam deus ipse regit."
<theodulf. carm. 28.455>	His aliquantisper monitis verbisque morare,
<theodulf. carm. 28.456>	Gustumque egregium legis ab amne dabis.
<theodulf. carm. 28.457>	At si forte levi ventosa Superbia nisu
<theodulf. carm. 28.458>	Te petere affectet, te lacerare velit;
<theodulf. carm. 28.459>	Torva oculos, horrenda manus, fedissima rictus,
<theodulf. carm. 28.460>	Vipereumque caput, corpus et omne tumens,
